WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.772 line:0%
Hi, my name is Howard Forman.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:09.075 line:0%
I'm a physician and a professor
at the Yale School of Public

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.344 line:0%
Health and Yale
School of Management.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:14.314 line:0%
I'd like to talk about one
method of protecting people

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:17.417 line:0%
from COVID-19 that's been
getting some attention,

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.418 line:0%
herd immunity.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:25.191
In simple terms, herd immunity
is communal protection from

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:29.029
a disease, we achieve it
once a large proportion of a

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:33.533
population is immune to the
disease and presumably the

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.603
ability to spread
it. Dramatically reducing the

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:39.639
risk of spread to
others who are not immune.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:42.942
You can think of it as the
percentage of a population that

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.645
must be immune
to extend immunity

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.747
to others automatically.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:50.784 line:0%
The safest way to
do this is through vaccination.

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:51.851
Through vaccines,

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:55.388
we have achieved herd immunity
to many dangerous diseases,

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:59.559
including measles,
whooping cough and chicken pox.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:07.534
Isolated incidents can
still occur, but it means a

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:10.637
major outbreak
is highly unlikely.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:14.040
Before vaccines herd immunity
was achieved naturally

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.942
but brutally.
Disease would

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.243
spread unchecked,

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:20.447
survivors would develop
antibodies and immunity.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:24.117
Eventually, enough people would
be immune to halt spread until

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:28.188
new unimmunized members of
society were introduced

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.523
generally via
birth or migration,

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:33.526
and then outbreaks
could occur again.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:43.269
In the case of the virus that
causes covid-19, achieving herd

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.806
immunity without a vaccine
would require allowing up to 70

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:50.343
percent of the US population
to become infected.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:53.012
That's two hundred and thirty
one million people.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:56.149
And since zero point four
percent of those individuals at

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:59.752
the lowest estimate would die,
we would lose close to one

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.388
million Americans and leave
countless others with

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.424
longstanding health problems.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:08.161
This violates a central tenet
of biomedical ethics:

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.031
To achieve herd immunity to

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.367
COVID-19 through vaccination,

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:18.438
a substantial percent of the
population must be vaccinated,

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:21.741
perhaps as high as
70 percent of those eligible.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.781
through patience and by
employing various strategies to

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.851
manage COVID-19's spread,
